hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1322","Narrated to us Muhammad bin Rafi’, narrated to us Al-Mu’mal bin Ismail, narrated to us Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One of the signs of the Hour is that people will brag about their mosques.”"
"1323","Narrated by Muhammad bin Yahya, narrated by Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i, narrated by Hammad, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, and Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Hour will not come until people show off in the mosques.”"
